  "transferStationNote": "Two rules, two questions. 'sameStation' (server, 1 km) decides GROUPING: do these trains form one ride? Paris Est and Paris Nord, 500 m apart, rightly do. 'transferStation' (web, 150 m) decides what the transfer line says: must the traveller go to another station? For the same pair the answer is yes, and 'kein Bahnhofswechsel' would be a false statement a traveller acts on. 150 m covers one station's own records (a geocoder pick beside its catalogue row), not its neighbours. The display threshold must stay inside the grouping one: a pair the transfer line calls the same station must also group.",
